# Gate step 1158-y3ad — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# lww_entries folds two channel spellings; three consumers in main.rs read one.
# A `fields:`-spelled write was invisible to all three, and the two failure
# symptoms are OPPOSITE: silent in the scans that look for offenders, LOUD (a
# false advisory about a packet whose next_action WAS set) in the scan that
# looks for an omission. Neither says `fields:`.
#
# The behavioural arms pin the three sites; the scan-side arm is what stops a
# fourth consumer being written that hardcodes one spelling again.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
